@startuml client-submit-express-order
title Client submits express order

actor "Submitting client" as client
participant "order-intake" as intake
database "orders-db" as db
queue "order-events" as topic
participant "fulfilment-service" as fulfil

== Happy path ==
client -> intake : 1. POST /orders\nIdempotency-Key; client timeout 30 s
intake -> db : 2. Find key; timeout 50 ms
db --> intake : 3. Not found
intake -> db : 4. Commit order + key + outbox; timeout 70 ms
db --> intake : 5. Committed — order is durable
intake --> client : 6. 202 Accepted + status URL
intake ->> topic : 7. Outbox relay publishes order.accepted
topic ->> fulfil : 8. At-least-once delivery; dedup by messageId
fulfil -> intake : 9. PUT internal state; timeout 500 ms, max 3 retries
intake -> db : 10. Idempotently update state by eventId

== Duplicate submission ==
client -> intake : POST /orders with same key
intake -> db : Find key
db --> intake : Original order id
intake --> client : 202 Accepted + original status URL

== Database unavailable ==
client -> intake : POST /orders
intake ->x db : Timeout
intake --> client : 503 + Retry-After
note over client : Retry with the same key is safe.

== Publish or fulfilment unavailable ==
intake ->x topic : Relay publish fails
note over intake : Outbox remains pending; relay retries with backoff.
topic ->x fulfil : Consumer unavailable
note over topic : Messages accumulate; alert when lag > 5 min.

== Poison message ==
topic ->> fulfil : order.accepted
fulfil -> fulfil : Processing fails; 3 attempts with backoff and jitter
fulfil ->> topic : Move to DLQ
note right of fulfil : DLQ depth > 0 pages Fulfilment.\nOPEN: drain runbook before production.

== Terminal outcomes ==
note over client,fulfil
Success: accepted and processed.
Partial: accepted, awaiting retry or in DLQ.
Failure: 503, no order committed.
Timed out: client retries with the same key.
end note

@enduml
